# Defect 451, 2026-10-08, the read beside the write. Symptom: C reading
# through the address of an `@` local after the local's function had
# returned read what the region still held, the 1 it had written, at exit 0
# at `-O0`, `-O2` and under `--sanitize` at both (measured on this Mac at
# `56def9b4`). Cause: a region given back stayed readable.
#
# A KNOWN COST OF THE PLAIN BUILDS, PINNED: they watch a region given back
# by the sum of its bytes, which a read does not move, so the plain runs
# still read the 1 (`runtime/parts/lend.c`, WHAT A PLAIN BUILD CANNOT SEE);
# sealing every room in every build would see it, at x7.8 to x18.4 the
# instructions of a loop that lends. Under `--sanitize` a region given back
# is sealed, so the read faults where C makes it and AddressSanitizer names
# it. A plain build that comes to see it turns this case red, and its
# expectation is then written again.

extern "fixedbugs-451-keepers.h"
    function cell_keep(@out: i64)
    function cell_read_later() -> i64

function lend() -> i64
    n: i64 @ 0
    cell_keep(@n)
    return n

function main()
    print(lend())
    print(cell_read_later())
